  13:     - bg = most common color.
  14:     - Border-touching components cluster into anchor frames with interior bg cavities.
  15:     - Non-border 2-color components are movable tools.
  16: 
  17:     Rule:
  18:     - Match each tool to a frame whose cavity size equals one of its color-region counts.
  19:     - Rotate/flip the tool so one color fills the cavity exactly; the other stays outside.
  20:     - If the docking orientation uses a reflection, swap the tool's two colors.
  21: 
  22:     Key insight: Cavity size determines tool–frame pairing; reflection triggers color swap.
